{
  "dom_id": "step-q143620",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{5}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{4}{3}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{5}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{4}{3}) & ={\\int }_{1/5}^{1}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{4}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/5}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1/5}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
